  "scenarioProofNotes": {
    "door-landings": "1010.1.6 ordinary 44-inch travel length and individual R-2 unit 36-inch exception; width/swing restrictions remain distinct.",
    "bathtub-outlets": "407.2 requires both outlets, 1.5-inch connection and watertight waste stopper.",
    "bathroom-oil-appliance": "303.3 prohibited-room predicate and all three enumerated exceptions reviewed. Direct-vent exception excludes sleeping rooms, requires all combustion air outdoors and listing/manufacturer installation.",
    "gas-meter-valve": "409.2 places utility-approved valve upstream, not merely on either side of meter.",
    "sprinkler-visual-records": "901.6.2.1 monthly certificate-of-fitness visual inspection and all defects/violations on report. No unsupported imported NFPA periodic-testing schedule is asserted.",
    "accessible-ramp": "1012.1 means-of-egress ramp scope; 1012.2 ordinary 1:12 running slope and exceptions; 1012.3 1:48 cross slope; 1012.4 30-inch run rise. Garage/assembly/curb scenarios expressly excluded.",
    "terrace-guard": "1015.2 >30-inch vertical drop at any point within 36 inches horizontally; initial at-grade terrace avoids independent rooftop applicability. Exactly 30 inches does not trigger this predicate. Loading-side dock exception is narrowly applied.",
    "shower-waterproofing": "417.5.2 full liner scope/exceptions and 2-inch turn-up/1-inch perforation threshold; 312.9 plugged drain, potable water, 2-inch threshold-measured depth, temporary threshold when needed, at least 15 minutes, no leakage.",
    "restaurant-grease": "1003.3.1 applies to FOG waste from food-preparation fixtures and restricts interceptor inflow to fixtures/equipment allowing FOG discharge; ordinary toilet waste is outside that fixture purpose. 1003.3.3 dwelling/private-quarters/non-culinary-school exceptions reviewed; keys assert no DEP size without DEP rules.",
    "condensate-protection": "307.2 cooling equipment scope and sensible-only exception; 307.2.1 slope/disposal; 307.2.3 damage predicate, four allowed methods and both exceptions. Method 3 pan construction and listed shutdown device conditions retained; no floor-drain exception assumed.",
    "dryer-duct": "504.8 domestic scope; 504.8.1 smooth metal thickness/diameter/manufacturer larger-size condition; 504.8.2 1/8-inch fastener limit, 4-foot supports, secured joints/direction. Permanent duct explicitly distinguished from transition duct. No duct-length table claim is made.",
    "gas-shutoff-access": "409.1.2 concealment/plenum prohibition, 409.1.3 access plus damage protection, 409.5.2 vented decorative remote-location exception with ready access/dedicated/identified valve and stated piping qualification. Chapter 401-408 design contents are not inferred.",
    "gas-restoration": "406.6 scope and 406.6.1 pressure-test prerequisite; 406.6.3 initial restoration leakage check, shutoff until repairs and allowed testing methods; 406.5.2 affected-system repairs/retest; 406.7.1.4 instrument requirements read. Earlier pressure test is not treated as operating leak check.",
    "rooftop-access": "504.4 <=100-foot roof and <=20-degree slope predicates; 504.4.4 6-foot width and 9-foot height; 504.4.6 six-foot door clearance measured from hinge. Actual current parent includes operative rooftop qualifiers and later amendments; no perimeter landing/parapet datum is substituted for path height.",
    "emergency-light-tests": "1027.9 lighting maintenance scope; 1027.9.1 >=30-second monthly manual activation or automated feature with monthly visual inspection; 1027.9.2 >=90-minute annual battery test, qualified person, 604.5 dependency. Manual/visual/power tests remain separate.",
    "office-loading-table": "36-62 current two-column loading table and category mapping reviewed against official DCP page. Supplied Use Group VII/LRC-C and C4-4 select the second district column: first100k none, next200k one, each additional300k one. First, corrected and enlarged total areas are stated development scenarios; no waiver or other use assumed.",
    "residential-parking-location": "25-621(c) multiple-dwelling location rule includes street-wall prolongations, through-lot limitation along only one frontage, entire-block and large-site exceptions. R7 avoids lower-density-area replacement. Narrow location approval does not approve yards/curb cuts or entire parking design."
